Table~\ref{tab:mosi} shows that no fusion style beats text alone on MOSI. With the style
chosen on held-out data, accuracy $H$ is $-1.60$ ($[-3.10,-0.10]$, $p=0.042$). On MOSEI
it is $+0.29$ ($[-0.38,+0.97]$, $p=0.29$). Held-out data cannot separate early from mid
fusion on either corpus (held-out accuracy $99.18$ vs.\ $99.41$ on MOSI, $71.19$ vs.\
$71.20$ on MOSEI); counted with early fusion, $H$ is $-1.06$ ($p=0.12$) and $+0.86$
($[+0.27,+1.45]$, $p=0.016$). Selecting hyper-parameters per configuration gives $-1.12$
($p=0.068$) and $+1.04$ ($p=0.057$). Either way, fusion adds nothing measurable on MOSI and
about one point at most on MOSEI.

Selection matters. Late averaging posts the highest MOSEI test accuracy, $+1.51$ over
text with $p=0.002$, yet ranks last among the fusion styles on held-out accuracy
($65.16$). Choosing the fusion style by its test mean would have reported a gain between
$1.8$ and $5$ times larger than the ones the held-out data support.

The floor bites here too. The best constant predictor scores $62.10$ accuracy on MOSI,
so audio-only and video-only both score \emph{below} a classifier that ignores its input.
MOSI's training majority is negative and its test majority positive, so a constant
predictor fit to the training split scores $37.90$ --- the same formula, $24$ points
apart, depending on which $\pi_0$ is used.

\subsection{MELD with Frozen Encoders}\label{sec:meld}

The MELD rows of Table~\ref{tab:headroom} rest on the features released with that paper,
and a weak unimodal baseline biases $H$ upward. MELD's raw media are public, so this can
be tested. We re-extracted MELD with encoders that never saw a MELD label and were never
fine-tuned: BERT-base~\cite{devlin2019} on the official transcripts and
WavLM-base-plus~\cite{chen2022wavlm} on the audio of each clip, mean-pooled over the last
layer ($2$ of $13{,}708$ clips have no media). The protocol is that of the previous
subsection, training on the official training and development dialogues and testing on
the official test split. Text and audio are the modalities of the published rows.

